{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/968621-exorcism-question-for-2nd-edition","id":968621,"title":"Exorcism Question for 2nd edition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-13T11:02:01-07:00","id":968621,"title":"Exorcism Question for 2nd edition","content":"Looking at the rules for summoning and exorcism, I need some clarification. The research roles described reveal an entities bane or ban. The summoning/exorcising portion says the same roll (intelligence + occult) is needed to discover how to create the proper conditions, and that exorcism is just un-doing the proper conditions. So my question is...what does that look like game mechanics wise? I understand researching a fire spirit's bane might be something obvious like water. Is that all an exorcism is - Using a bane to touch a possessed person or using an abjuration? So an exorcism can be pretty fast if the right bane has been discovered and the entity fails its roll to stay in the person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/19.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12209-adonus","name":"adonus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T11:17:50-07:00","id":968630,"title":"","content":"Apart from Bane and Ban, research can also help identify a ghost's Anchor or the conditions necessary to make something Resonant with a spirit. By removing these, you can also break a possession (since they are prerequisites of the Open condition).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T11:21:55-07:00","id":968633,"title":"","content":"No, an exorcism is a series of actions to interact with the entity's prerequisite Conditions in an attempt to dismantle them. For example, if you're trying to remove a ghost from a house, you might do a reaearch roll to figure out what it's Anchor is, and another to find out what it has done in the house to advance the Anchor Condition to Open, then make a roll to undo that fine-tuning and bring the area back down to Anchor, and then finally salt and burn the anchor to send the ghost to the Underworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T11:34:59-07:00","id":968640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/968621-exorcism-question-for-2nd-edition?p=968633#post968633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, an exorcism is a series of actions to interact with the entity's prerequisite Conditions in an attempt to dismantle them. For example, if you're trying to remove a ghost from a house, you might do a reaearch roll to figure out what it's Anchor is, and another to find out what it has done in the house to advance the Anchor Condition to Open, then make a roll to undo that fine-tuning and bring the area back down to Anchor, and then finally salt and burn the anchor to send the ghost to the Underworld.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Bane can still provide a good incentive to leave, though, since it suffers wounds if its host comes into contact with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T11:52:55-07:00","id":968653,"title":"","content":"Ok, so using the ghost example. A ghost exists in a house, and its anchor is a hair-brush. The ghost influences anyone in the area to dwell upon him in whatever fashion. Soon the loved ones start to dwell on him all the time, putting up pictures and what not. Eventually the house becomes open and the ghost can freely manifest in the home. Our brave ghostfacers have researched the loved one, and know his precious hair-brush still exists, but they can't find it; also his spirit is appearing and beating them up. An exorcism research action would be to somehow find out what the ghost did to the home/loved ones. So lets say they notice there is practically a shrine to the man in the house, and on good intuition from an educated guess, they turn around all the pictures so no one sees the ghost. Would this be a good example of downgrading an open condition so the ghost can't manifest so they can find the anchor without getting the snot beat out of them? Or maybe even a prayer session thrown in to abjure the spirit when it manifests or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/19.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12209-adonus","name":"adonus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T12:20:42-07:00","id":968671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adonus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/968621-exorcism-question-for-2nd-edition?p=968653#post968653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, so using the ghost example. A ghost exists in a house, and its anchor is a hair-brush. The ghost influences anyone in the area to dwell upon him in whatever fashion. Soon the loved ones start to dwell on him all the time, putting up pictures and what not. Eventually the house becomes open and the ghost can freely manifest in the home. Our brave ghostfacers have researched the loved one, and know his precious hair-brush still exists, but they can't find it; also his spirit is appearing and beating them up. An exorcism research action would be to somehow find out what the ghost did to the home/loved ones. So lets say they notice there is practically a shrine to the man in the house, and on good intuition from an educated guess, they turn around all the pictures so no one sees the ghost. Would this be a good example of downgrading an open condition so the ghost can't manifest so they can find the anchor without getting the snot beat out of them? Or maybe even a prayer session thrown in to abjure the spirit when it manifests or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Excellent example! Yes, that would totally work. Note though that you don't abjure the ghost, you abjure his prerequisite Conditions to temporarily suppress them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}